{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ec01e32de2308100dd968926cff4235c86aa1743312953d2d776d1e4d2f56dd5","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira Data Center transport","key_entities":["_with_connection_retry","transport.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/retry.py","_errors.parse_retry_after","MAX_BACKOFF_S","_as_backend_http_error","create_issue","add_comment","add_label","_paged_search","get_comment_map","transition_issue_by_name","BackendHTTPError","jira.exceptions.JIRAError","TlsVerificationError","_tls_verification_error"],"problem_keywords":["rate-limit","429","Retry-After","Data Center","token bucket","retry policy","idempotent reads","mutations","duplicate-issue"],"propositions":["Jira Data Center rate-limit headers (Retry-After) are not honoured; a 429 response causes hard failure on first occurrence rather than retry","The retry mechanism must be scoped to idempotent reads only; retrying 429s on mutations through the shared _with_connection_retry choke point would reintroduce duplicate-issue bugs because 429 can arrive after server begins a write","The transport.py module is at locked 800-line capacity with only 11 lines headroom, requiring the retry/error cluster to be extracted to a separate module before 429 policy can be added","Retry-After values must be parsed with jitter (0-20% random) then clamped to MAX_BACKOFF_S maximum, and the per-call opt-in for 429 retry must default to OFF to prevent mutations from inheriting retry by omission"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787751162809668001,"uuid":"fd377be9-0a7b-4f77-aee2-c53a4b54af7b"}